{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Arise.</b> Know that the verbal noun is in every past or future verb, and even though it is not [so], sometimes it is written as such, like: וברך (and he blessed), and [in another form] לא אשיבנה. The meaning is וברך ברכה (and blessed a blessing), and likewise וברוב יועצים עצה תקום. And likewise כי הכית את כל אויבי לחי — either a bet is lacking, like הנמצא בית ה', כי ששת ימים עשה — and פנה הוא בלחי." "And the meaning of ושיני רשעים — corresponding to the many who say [it] to my soul, then it will be clear to all that the salvation is HaShem's, for He saves whomever He wills." "And the meaning of על עמך — they are those who fight on David's behalf, for they are the people of HaShem in truth, and not so those who aid the son to rise up against his father. And behold, he prayed that HaShem would bless them and that not a man of them would be lacking in battle — or he prophesied."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The phrase ולא אשיבנה is cited from 1 Samuel 15:29; the word לחי refers to Psalms 3:7 (הכית את כל אויבי לחי). The syntactic thread connecting the cited examples is compressed and opaque in the original; translated hyper-literally without smoothing.", 2 "Reading ולא יפקד as 'and not a man will be lacking,' following the idiom of לא יפקד מכם איש (Numbers 31:49)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:19.848574346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}